torch.use_deterministic_algorithms() ``` it does not flag pytorch operations that are not deterministic as mentioned in the [reproducibility  docs ](https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/notes/randomness.html). Its mentioned [here](https://github.com/facebookresearch/detectron2/issues/4723) that atomic add in roi align is most likely the issue. We should at least mention these in the docs for popular vision models so that we can make an informed opinion if the said model training is deterministic or not and if they will be fixed in the future following the guides by pytorch. 
 It would be great if more each vision model we have a placeholder of determinism its a critical component in using pytorch in production or in research.

